  "base": "Execute three phases in order. PHASE 1: emit public assistant text starting with BEGIN on its own line, followed by 400-450 harmless printable ASCII characters on one line. In this same turn, actually call acceptance_wait with stage BEGIN, then stop generating and wait for its real tool result. Do not mention MIDDLE or STREAM yet. PHASE 2 starts only after the first successful tool result: emit new public text starting with MIDDLE on its own line, followed by 400-450 harmless printable ASCII characters on one line. Actually call acceptance_wait with stage MIDDLE, then stop generating and wait for its real result. PHASE 3 starts only after both successful tool results: output exactly 100 literal lines STREAM001 through STREAM100, in order, each prefix immediately followed by 80-120 harmless printable ASCII characters. The full literal template below is authoritative for PHASE 3 only. After both successful wait results, emit its contents verbatim as your public assistant answer, from STREAM001 through the final marker. Copy the entire template exactly; do not generate your own lines, count aloud, annotate, repair or extend it. The opening and closing template delimiters are NOT part of the answer. The template uses this exact 100-character suffix once per line: abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv. No extra prose, ellipses or code fences. End with O4E_INSPECT_ACCEPTANCE_DONE on its own final line and nothing after it. Stop immediately after the marker; no self-review, explanation, correction, repeated marker or extra prose before or after the template. The entire PHASE 3 public output, including all prefixes, newlines and the final marker, MUST be at most 16 KiB (16384 bytes). Only PHASE 3 forbids further tool calls; PHASES 1 and 2 REQUIRE real acceptance_wait calls, not text describing them. Emit all three phases as public assistant text, never reasoning or arguments as a substitute. Public progress must precede its call. Do not use tools or code to generate or rewrite the text. Each acceptance_wait performs a fixed 45-second wait, not Bash. Stop on any failed call; do not retry, skip a phase or claim success. No shell, files, network, delegation, Skills or workflows.\n\n<PHASE_3_OUTPUT_TEMPLATE>\nSTREAM001abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM002abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM003abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM004abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM005abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM006abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM007abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM008abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM009abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM010abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM011abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM012abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM013abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM014abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM015abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuv\nSTREAM016abcdefghijklmno